@page "/terms"
@inject ConsentVersions Consent

<PageTitle>Terms of Use</PageTitle>
<h1>Terms of Use</h1>

<p class="muted">Version @_versions.Terms</p>

<h2>What this is</h2>
<p>
    cv-maker builds a typeset CV from facts you enter, optionally tailored to a job posting you
    paste. It is offered as-is, with no guarantee of availability, and it is not a
    career-advice service.
</p>

<h2>What it will not do</h2>
<p>
    Generated content is checked against your profile before it becomes a document: anything
    that cannot be traced back to a fact you entered is rejected rather than printed. That check
    is the point of the product, and it is also its limit — it proves a claim came from you, not
    that the claim is true. <strong>Read what you send.</strong> You are responsible for the
    accuracy of your own CV.
</p>

<h2>Your account</h2>
<ul>
    <li>You need a working email address, and you are responsible for what happens under your account.</li>
    <li>One person per account. Do not share credentials.</li>
    <li>You can delete your data at any time from <a href="account">Your data</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Fair use</h2>
<p>
    Generation costs real money per document. Please do not automate bulk generation, resell
    access, or use the service to produce documents for other people at scale. Accounts doing
    that may be limited or closed.
</p>

<h2>Pasted content</h2>
<p>
    Only paste job adverts you are applying to. Do not paste anything confidential, and do not
    paste other people's personal data beyond what the advert itself contains. Pasted postings
    are deleted after 30 days — see the <a href="privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
</p>

<h2>Your content is yours</h2>
<p>
    You keep every right in the facts you enter and the CVs you generate. Storing and processing
    them to run the service is the only permission this grants, and it ends when you delete
    them.
</p>

<h2>The templates</h2>
<p>
    The CV templates carry their own licences. The <em>altacv-modern</em> template embeds
    <code>altacv.cls</code> by LianTze Lim, distributed under the LaTeX Project Public Licence.
    Generating a document with it is ordinary use; redistributing the template is governed by
    that licence.
</p>

<h2>Liability</h2>
<p>
    The service is provided without warranty. It is not liable for a job you did not get, a
    document that failed to generate, or data lost to an outage. Keep your own copy of anything
    that matters.
</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>
    These terms are versioned. A change that affects you means being asked to accept the new
    version rather than being moved onto it quietly.
</p>

@code {
    private ConsentVersions.Versions _versions = new("…", "…", "…");

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() => _versions = await Consent.GetAsync();
}
